hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24050","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated to us Shubah, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from a man of Aslam, that he was stung, and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you had said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed you. Suhayl said: So my father, if one of us was stung, would say: Did he say it? If they said: Yes, he said: As if he sees that it will not harm him."
"24051","Narrated to us Abu Kamil, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Saad, narrated to us Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is imminent that Luka ibn Luka will dominate the world, and the best of people is a believer between two noble ones. He did not raise it."
